## Engine and viewport matrix

| Project | Device profile | Runs |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `desktop-chromium` | Desktop Chrome 1280x720 | all suites, including `seo`, `layout`, `rendering` |
| `desktop-firefox` | Desktop Firefox 1280x720 | `smoke`, `a11y`, `motion`, `navigation`, `footer`, `hero`, `service-strip`, `introduction`, `services`, `why`, `industries`, `work`, `process`, `page-hero`, `contact`, `detail-pages`, `about`, `pricing` |
| `desktop-webkit` | Desktop Safari 1280x720 | `smoke`, `a11y`, `motion`, `navigation`, `footer`, `hero`, `service-strip`, `introduction`, `services`, `why`, `industries`, `work`, `process`, `page-hero`, `contact`, `detail-pages`, `about`, `pricing` |
| `mobile-chromium` | Pixel 7 emulation | `smoke`, `a11y`, `motion`, `navigation`, `footer`, `hero`, `service-strip`, `introduction`, `services`, `why`, `industries`, `work`, `process`, `page-hero`, `contact`, `detail-pages`, `about`, `pricing` |
| `mobile-webkit` | iPhone 15 emulation | `smoke`, `a11y`, `motion`, `navigation`, `footer`, `hero`, `service-strip`, `introduction`, `services`, `why`, `industries`, `work`, `process`, `page-hero`, `contact`, `detail-pages`, `about`, `pricing` |

Engine-independent suites (metadata, static assets, viewport layout) run once in desktop Chromium on purpose; do not add them to the other projects. Mobile projects are browser emulations, not physical devices.

## Running

- Routine: `npm run test:e2e:chromium` (desktop and mobile Chromium).
- Full matrix: `npm run test:e2e` (rebuilds `dist/` first, serves it on port 4322).
- One suite or project: `npx playwright test tests/e2e/layout.spec.ts --project=desktop-chromium`.
- Debug: `npm run test:e2e:ui`; last report: `npm run test:e2e:report`.
- Against an existing build without rebuilding: `PLAYWRIGHT_SKIP_BUILD=1 npx playwright test`.
- Browsers are installed once with `npx playwright install chromium firefox webkit`.
- The web server command is `astro preview --port 4322 --ignore-lock`: Astro 7 would otherwise detach the server into the background when run by an agent, and Playwright could not stop it. Keep the flag and the port (4321 is the dev server).

## Engine notes

- WebKit mirrors Safari: plain Tab skips links. Tests that must reach a link in WebKit press `Alt+Tab` (Option+Tab); this is engine behaviour, not a site defect.
- Playwright's WebKit is newer than the Safari visitors run, so it can pass where Safari fails: Safari 27.2 left the navbar call to action's aura lit after the pointer left, from a repaint bug WebKit fixed on 2026-10-09. Check paint and motion changes in Safari itself, and test the mechanism where the engine cannot show the bug (the navigation suite's "fades through its strength" test).
- A Playwright WebKit screenshot breaks a running transition of an `@property` custom property: afterwards the computed value reads the end value while the transition still runs, so the shot shows a finished fade. Sample such fades with `getComputedStyle` across animation frames, or record a video, not with screenshots.
- Firefox is Playwright's bundled build. On macOS 27.2 it fails to start ("Could not find profile folder") with or without a sandbox; run the rest of the matrix with `PLAYWRIGHT_SKIP_FIREFOX=1 npm run test:e2e`, then run Firefox in the Linux container described in `docs/quality-checks.md`, or state in the report that Firefox ran only in CI (Ubuntu). Never skip it silently.
- CI runs on Linux, which still differs from macOS: WebKit styles the page once before the stylesheet arrives, and before Catamaran and Mukta load the generic fallback is DejaVu Sans. After those files load, both platforms draw the same families, but Chromium on Linux hints small type and rounds each letter up to whole pixels, so 10-13px bold text sets up to a sixth wider than on a Mac. Text placed to the pixel needs `text-rendering: geometricPrecision`, as the hero orbit's names have (in the `orbit` utility); without it "WordPress" ran off a 320px screen in CI (2026-11-18). A macOS pass does not show that CI passes; reproduce platform-specific failures in the Linux container.
- Playwright 1.65's Firefox (159) crashes the page ("Page crashed", signal 11) when `evaluateAll` runs on a locator inside a region found by its name after anything else has queried that region, such as a count, an expect, or an `evaluate`. To read the boxes of many elements in such a region, run one `evaluate` on their container (`itemBoxes` in `tests/e2e/service-strip.spec.ts`), or use a CSS locator not chained from the named region.
- Under `javaScriptEnabled: false`, never assert with `toHaveJSProperty`: it is the one matcher Playwright evaluates in the page's own script world, which Firefox does not provide while JavaScript is off, so the expect never answers and the test runs into its timeout (CI run 44825131550, 2026-11-20, in `detail-pages.spec.ts`). Every other matcher runs in Playwright's utility world and works. Assert what the visitor sees instead: a `details` that has opened carries `open=""` (`toHaveAttribute('open', '')`) and its answer `toBeVisible()`.

## Writing tests

- Add a focused spec for each new interactive island or form (`tests/e2e/<feature>.spec.ts`). A test that walks every built route sets its timeout from the route count (`test.setTimeout(routes.length * …)`), as the a11y, seo, rendering, motion, layout, and page-hero suites do, so adding pages never trips the 30-second default. Page-level metadata, layout, and accessibility are already covered by the site-wide suites, so do not duplicate those assertions.
- Locate elements by role and accessible name (`getByRole('button', { name: /send/i })`), then by label or text. Avoid CSS selectors tied to Tailwind classes.
- Use web-first assertions (`await expect(locator).toBeVisible()`); never `waitForTimeout`.
- Test behaviour visible to the user: navigation opens and closes with keyboard, form validation messages appear and are associated with fields, filters change the list. Do not test third-party services; for Netlify Forms assert the hidden `form-name` input and attributes, and answer the form's POST from the test with `page.route` (`answerWith` in `tests/e2e/contact.spec.ts`) rather than letting it reach a server.
- Keep tests independent and deterministic; no shared mutable state between tests.
- Mark temporary skips with a reason: `test.skip(condition, 'reason')`, and remove them before finishing.

## Screenshots

`reports/screenshots/` holds inspection screenshots written by the layout suite and by manual checks. They are gitignored and are not visual-regression baselines; look at them and describe what you saw. If visual regression testing is adopted later, baselines must be reviewed on every change, never regenerated to make a failure disappear.

## When a check fails

Read the failing step's name (route, width, or action), reproduce locally with `--ui` if needed, fix the page rather than loosening the assertion. Thresholds in the SEO, layout, and accessibility suites change only with a documented decision in `docs/quality-checks.md`.
